## What this lane was

Two deliverables: (1) THE CATALOG — a GENERATED document
`docs/THE_LIBRARY.md` plus its pure generator
`tools/creature_graph/library_catalog.py`; (2) the acceptance sweep,
`acceptance.py --offline`, every item ending repaired or recorded.

## Deliverable 1: the catalog

`tools/creature_graph/library_catalog.py` loads the live sharded store
(`CreatureGraph.load()`, bulk shards merged automatically) and emits
markdown through one pure function (`build_catalog`: graph in → markdown
out; sorted iteration, no clock, no locale, no environment text). The
document contains NO hand-written facts:

- one section per admitted source (id, manifest identity, license quoted
  verbatim from the record's own manifest, record counts by kind,
  quarantine counts with top refusal causes + first detail, deferred
  records with causes, receipt fields embedded in the record (bundle_id,
  count-identity law quoted), class contracts used with registry sha
  prefixes, known gaps from the record, and a per-source **record-set
  digest** — sha256 over the canonical JSON of every cited record, so ANY
  byte change to ANY cited record moves the doc);
- a summary table: source × records × license-class × auth-class (the
  license class is a documented substring bookkeeping label over the
  record's own quoted license text; the quote is the authoritative fact);
- standing gaps: the four gaps quoted verbatim from the graph record
  `work.data.batch_intake` → `observation.database_hunt_20260917.
  gaps_that_still_stand` (joint morphology, quadruped EMG, bulk
  tribology, fur BRDF) with the owning record cited;
- batch receipts cited by graph records (whole-batch receipt path +
  sha256 + batch_id from `work.data.batch_intake.observation`);
- "How to admit the next database": the `batch_qualify` command shape,
  connector/contract file pointers, and the count-identity law.

Library measured: **19 admitted source objects, 33,417 records** (note:
two databases were admitted twice through distinct pinned bundles —
PanTHERIA, and the soil/GSOD/THOR/WorldCover re-batches — so source
OBJECTS outnumber distinct databases; that duplication is reported
honestly, never silently merged). Deferred records in-store: 0 (the
`batch.deferred.dryad_file` class exists but holds no records in this
store). Largest sources: Rhea 14,202; PanTHERIA 9,531; BodyParts3D 3,432
(841 quarantined label conflicts); IAEA LiveChart 3,386.

## Rule 0 (and a recorded defect)

The falsifier was banked BEFORE the generator existed: revision 1 of
`work.data.library_catalog_20260918` (statement / prediction /
falsifier, status `untested`) via the idempotent, revision-aware
`tools/creature_graph/validation/admit_library_catalog_20260918.py`,
then `build_graph.py` rebuild. **Process defect, recorded on the record
itself:** revision 2 (status `tested`) shipped in the same file as
revision 1, so the FIRST script run banked the tested-status record
before the generator/tests existed — the statement was prior to any run,
the status claim was not. Repaired by revision 3: the defect is written
into the record (`physical.contract.process_defect_recorded`) and the
outcomes are timestamped to the actual test runs. The revision-aware
replace path (revisions 1 and 2 are recognized priors) is what made the
honest rewrite possible; idempotency re-verified (second run = no-op).

Falsifier as tests (`tools/creature_graph/tests/test_library_catalog.py`,
6 tests, OK): byte-identity regeneration from the live store; mutation
sensitivity (record-name flip on a bulk-shard record, quarantine-code
flip, license flip — all change the catalog bytes, targeted counts move;
plus fixture-graph record-add/quarantine-add count movement); every count
in the doc equals an independent recount from the store (totals, summary
rows, per-kind, per-source quarantine, gap strings, receipt citations,
every cited source id exists); the committed `docs/THE_LIBRARY.md` equals
a fresh regeneration. Test rules follow `tests/harness.py`: temp
workspaces only, the canonical data dir is never written.

